ually, B is small (1 or 2), H is small too (8-20). PyTorch overhead per matmul call should be negligible vs the compute time.\n\nLet me try yet another idea: can we express `||p_mix @ x|| / ||p1 @ x||` in terms of something else? \n\n`ratio = ||p1@x|| / ||p_mix@x||`\n`r = clamp(ratio, 0.25, 4.0)`\n`y = r * (p_mix @ v)`\n\nWhat if we compute everything in terms of p1 as the base?\n`p_mix = (1-β)*p0 + β*p1`\n`m = p_mix @ x = (1-β)*u0 + β*u1`\n\nNot helpful for reducing compute.\n\nOK, let me try a completely different approach. Let me see if computing logits in a different layout helps — specifically, what if we keep everything in (B, H, L, *) layout and use batched operations consistently?\n\nActually, let me try something practical. Let me write a version that:\n1. Computes G first (it's small and independent)\n2. Uses addmm_ for projections to avoid allocation overhead\n3. Computes p0@G and p1@G (so we have both), then uses quadratic formula for ||m||\n4. Computes output as (1-beta)*p0@v + beta*p1@v (avoiding p_mix allocation)\n5. Saves the lerp and p_mix allocation\n\nWait, but we still need the same number of matmuls. Let me just implement the cleanest, most in-place version and see.\n\nActually, I just want to try one more thing: what if instead of computing `p @ G` for norms, we compute `(p @ x).pow(2).sum(-1)` but use a smart contraction? No, that's the same as p@x then norm.\n\nLet me try one more radical idea: what if we can compute `||p@x|| / ||p@x||` ratios without full norms? Like, using the fact that softmax rows sum to 1?\n\n`p @ x` has rows that are convex combinations of rows of x (since p is softmax output, each row sums to 1 and is non-negative). So `row_i(p@x)` is inside the convex hull of rows of x. But that doesn't give us a way to compute norms faster.\n\nWhat about using `||p@x||_F^2 = trace(p @ G @ p^T) = sum of row-wise norms`?\nWe already compute row-wise norms via `(p@G * p).sum(-1)`. No improvement.\n\nAlright, let me try a practical implementation with a few focused optimizations and measure it:\n1. Compute G = x@x^T early (it's independent)\n2. Compute q, k, v using the most efficient projection method\n3. Use view-based softmax (already doing this)\n4. Compute norms via p1@G + p_mix@G (current approach, fastest)\n5. More in-place operations\n6. Use `torch.bmm` for reshaped 3D tensors (to potentially get better MKL batching)\n\nLet me also try one more thing I've been wondering about: what if we compute `p @ G` using `(p @ x) @ x^T` but don't materialize the full p@x? No, that requires computing p@x first which is the expensive direct method.\n\nLet me just implement the best version I can:\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat > /tmp/test_method.py << 'PYEOF'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Test optimized variant.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport math\nimport torch\n\n\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef attention_v1(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Current baseline.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    B, L, C = x.shape\n    H, D = wq.shape[0], wq.shape[1]\n    inv_sqrt_d = 1.0 / math.sqrt(D)\n    HD = H * D\n    BHL = B * H * L\n    xr = x.reshape(B * L, C)\n\n    q = (xr @ wq.reshape(HD, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    k = (xr @ wk.reshape(HD, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    v = (xr @ wv.reshape(HD, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n\n    logits = q @ k.transpose(-1, -2)\n    logits.mul_(inv_sqrt_d)\n\n    p0 = logits.view(BHL, L).softmax(dim=-1).view(B, H, L, L)\n\n    if alpha == 1.0:\n        y = p0 @ v\n    else:\n        a_p = 0.5 * (1.0 + alpha)\n        a_m = 0.5 * (1.0 - alpha)\n        p1_logits = logits.mul(a_p)\n        p1_logits.add_(logits.transpose(-1, -2), alpha=a_m)\n        p1 = p1_logits.view(BHL, L).softmax(dim=-1).view(B, H, L, L)\n\n        p_mix = torch.lerp(p0, p1, beta)\n\n        G = x @ x.transpose(-1, -2)\n        G_exp = G.unsqueeze(1)\n\n        p1G = p1 @ G_exp\n        norm1_sq = p1G.mul_(p1).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n        pmG = p_mix @ G_exp\n        normm_sq = pmG.mul_(p_mix).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n        norm1 = norm1_sq.sqrt_().clamp_min_(1e-6)\n        normm = normm_sq.sqrt_().clamp_min_(1e-6)\n        ratio = norm1.div_(normm).clamp_(0.25, 4.0)\n\n        y = (p_mix @ v).mul_(ratio)\n\n    return y.transpose(1, 2).flatten(2).contiguous()\n\n\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef attention_v2(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Optimized: precompute G, fused ops, p0@G + p1@G with quadratic ||m||, no p_mix.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    B, L, C = x.shape\n    H, D = wq.shape[0], wq.shape[1]\n    inv_sqrt_d = 1.0 / math.sqrt(D)\n    HD = H * D\n    BHL = B * H * L\n    xr = x.reshape(B * L, C)\n\n    # Precompute Gram matrix (independent of attention weights)\n    G = x @ x.transpose(-1, -2)\n    G_exp = G.unsqueeze(1)\n\n    # Projections\n    wq_r = wq.reshape(HD, C)\n    wk_r = wk.reshape(HD, C)\n    wv_r = wv.reshape(HD, C)\n\n    q = (xr @ wq_r.T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    k = (xr @ wk_r.T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    v = (xr @ wv_r.T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n\n    # Logits\n    logits = q @ k.transpose(-1, -2)\n    logits.mul_(inv_sqrt_d)\n\n    # p0 softmax\n    p0 = logits.view(BHL, L).softmax(dim=-1).view(B, H, L, L)\n\n    if alpha == 1.0:\n        y = p0 @ v\n    else:\n        a_p = 0.5 * (1.0 + alpha)\n        a_m = 0.5 * (1.0 - alpha)\n\n        # p1 logits + softmax\n        p1_logits = logits.mul(a_p)\n        p1_logits.add_(logits.transpose(-1, -2), alpha=a_m)\n        p1 = p1_logits.view(BHL, L).softmax(dim=-1).view(B, H, L, L)\n\n        # Compute p0 @ G and p1 @ G (two L\"'^3 matmuls, same as before)\n        p0G = p0 @ G_exp\n        p1G = p1 @ G_exp\n\n        # ||u0||''^2, ||u1||''^2, u0·u1\n        norm0_sq = p0G.mul_(p0).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n        norm1_sq = (p1 * p1G).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n        dot_01 = (p0 * p1G).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n\n        # ||m||''^2 = ||(1-beta)*u0 + beta*u1||''^2\n        b1 = 1.0 - beta\n        normm_sq = norm0_sq.mul_(b1 * b1)\n        normm_sq.add_(norm1_sq.mul(beta * beta))\n        normm_sq.add_(dot_01.mul_(2.0 * b1 * beta))\n\n        norm1 = norm1_sq.sqrt_().clamp_min_(1e-6)\n        normm = normm_sq.sqrt_().clamp_min_(1e-6)\n        ratio = norm1.div_(normm).clamp_(0.25, 4.0)\n\n        # Output: r * ((1-beta)*p0@v + beta*p1@v) = r * p_mix @ v\n        # Compute as r * (lerp(p0@v, p1@v, beta))\n        out0 = p0 @ v\n        out1 = p1 @ v\n        out = torch.lerp(out0, out1, beta)\n        y = out.mul_(ratio)\n\n    return y.transpose(1, 2).flatten(2).contiguous()\n\n\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef attention_v3(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta):\n    \"\"\"v2 but compute output via p_mix @ v (one matmul instead of two + lerp).\"\"\"\n    B, L, C = x.shape\n    H, D = wq.shape[0], wq.shape[1]\n    inv_sqrt_d = 1.0 / math.sqrt(D)\n    HD = H * D\n    BHL = B * H * L\n    xr = x.reshape(B * L, C)\n\n    G = x @ x.transpose(-1, -2)\n    G_exp = G.unsqueeze(1)\n\n    wq_r = wq.reshape(HD, C)\n    wk_r = wk.reshape(HD, C)\n    wv_r = wv.reshape(HD, C)\n\n    q = (xr @ wq_r.T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    k = (xr @ wk_r.T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    v = (xr @ wv_r.T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n\n    logits = q @ k.transpose(-1, -2)\n    logits.mul_(inv_sqrt_d)\n\n    p0 = logits.view(BHL, L).softmax(dim=-1).view(B, H, L, L)\n\n    if alpha == 1.0:\n        y = p0 @ v\n    else:\n        a_p = 0.5 * (1.0 + alpha)\n        a_m = 0.5 * (1.0 - alpha)\n\n        p1_logits = logits.mul(a_p)\n        p1_logits.add_(logits.transpose(-1, -2), alpha=a_m)\n        p1 = p1_logits.view(BHL, L).softmax(dim=-1).view(B, H, L, L)\n\n        # p_mix for output matmul\n        p_mix = torch.lerp(p0, p1, beta)\n\n        # Norms: p0@G + p1@G with quadratic formula for ||m||\n        p0G = p0 @ G_exp\n        p1G = p1 @ G_exp\n        norm0_sq = p0G.mul_(p0).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n        norm1_sq = (p1 * p1G).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n        dot_01 = (p0 * p1G).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n        b1 = 1.0 - beta\n        normm_sq = norm0_sq.mul_(b1 * b1)\n        normm_sq.add_(norm1_sq * (beta * beta))\n        normm_sq.add_(dot_01.mul_(2.0 * b1 * beta))\n\n        norm1 = norm1_sq.sqrt_().clamp_min_(1e-6)\n        normm = normm_sq.sqrt_().clamp_min_(1e-6)\n        ratio = norm1.div_(normm).clamp_(0.25, 4.0)\n\n        y = (p_mix @ v).mul_(ratio)\n\n    return y.transpose(1, 2).flatten(2).contiguous()\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    torch.set_num_threads(1)\n    import time\n\n    cases = [\n        (1, 64, 512, 8, 64, 1.05, 5.0),\n        (1, 128, 640, 10, 64, 1.1, 4.0),\n        (1, 128, 1280, 20, 64, 1.15, 3.0),\n        (1, 256, 1280, 20, 64, 1.05, 7.5),\n        (1, 256, 640, 10, 64, 1.2, 5.0),\n        (2, 128, 512, 8, 64, 1.0, 5.0),\n    ]\n\n    for idx, (B, L, C, H, D, alpha, beta) in enumerate(cases):\n        x = torch.randn(B, L, C)\n        wq = torch.randn(H, D, C)\n        wk = torch.randn(H, D, C)\n        wv = torch.randn(H, D, C)\n\n        # Warmup\n        for _ in range(3):\n            r1 = attention_v1(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\n            r2 = attention_v2(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\n            r3 = attention_v3(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\n\n        # Correctness\n        tol = 3e-5 + 3e-4 * r1.abs()\n        ok2 = ((r1 - r2).abs() <= tol).all().item()\n        ok3 = ((r1 - r3).abs() <= tol).all().item()\n        maxd2 = (r1 - r2).abs().max().item()\n        maxd3 = (r1 - r3).abs().max().item()\n\n        # Timing\n        N = 11\n        t0 = time.process_time_ns()\n        for _ in range(N):\n            attention_v1(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\n        t1 = time.process_time_ns()\n        v1_ms = (t1 - t0) / N / 1e6\n\n        t0 = time.process_time_ns()\n        for _ in range(N):\n            attention_v2(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\n        t1 = time.process_time_ns()\n        v2_ms = (t1 - t0) / N / 1e6\n\n        t0 = time.process_time_ns()\n        for _ in range(N):\n            attention_v3(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\n        t1 = time.process_time_ns()\n        v3_ms = (t1 - t0) / N / 1e6\n\n        print(f\"Case {idx} (B={B} L={L} C={C} H={H} alpha={alpha}):\")\n        print(f\"  v1 (current): {v1_ms:.2f} ms\")\n        print(f\"  v2 (quad_norm, 2 out matmuls): {v2_ms:.2f} ms ({v2_ms/v1_ms:.3f}x) ok={ok2} maxdiff={maxd2:.2e}\")\n        print(f\"  v3 (quad_norm, p_mix@v): {v3_ms:.2f} ms ({v3_ms/v1_ms:.3f}x) ok={ok3} maxdiff={maxd3:.2e}\")\nPYEOF\npython3 /tmp/test_method.py\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
